    trace.string_literal("Silent");
    trace.string_literal("Rage aim");
    trace.string_literal("Auto fire");
    trace.string_literal("##rage_left");
    trace.string_literal("##rage_right");
    trace.string_literal("Enable##rage");
    trace.string_literal("##rage_hotkey");
    trace.string_literal("Release anti-LSAC guards");
    trace.string_literal("Extrapolate unreachable targets");
    trace.string_literal("Held, not toggled. Unbound (0) means always on while enabled.");
    trace.string_literal("Write the angle into the command only. Off also moves your\\nactual view, which is visible to you and to spectators.");
    trace.string_literal("Pull the trigger whenever the weapon backend reports ready.\\nThere is no hitchance gate: with Nospread on the cone is no\\nlonger random, so a \\'chance\\' would be gating on a number that\\nstopped describing anything.");
    trace.string_literal("Runs BESIDE the legit aimbot, reusing its target selection,\\nbacktrack records, visibility and resolver -- only the policy\\ndiffers: no smoothing, no FOV cone, the angle is written on the\\ntick it exists.\\n\\nThis is loud. It is meant to be.");
    trace.string_literal("For targets the server refuses to rewind (fake laggers). Carries them\\nforward through the real movement code, in steps of their own command\\nbundle, to a pose the server is actually holding.\\nFalls back to cl_lagcompensation 0, which the server can see.");
    trace.string_literal("Turns aimbot_settings.anti_lsac OFF while rage is held and puts\\nYOUR value back the moment it is not -- the angle-delta limiter,\\nthe reversal check, the fake mouse deltas and the movement octant\\nsnap all hang off that one master.\\n\\nEvery one of them exists to make the aim look like a hand, and\\nevery one costs accuracy. In a rage fight the anti-aim has already\\ngiven that away.");
