    trace.string_literal("Apply in animation state");
    trace.string_literal("0 = auto (ping + interp).");
    trace.string_literal("Body side##aa_desync_side");
    trace.string_literal("Keep steering on cooldown");
    trace.string_literal("Relative to##aa_at_target");
    trace.string_literal("Ignore uninformative shots");
    trace.string_literal("Manual direction (toggles)");
    trace.string_literal("Seed brute from body signals");
    trace.string_literal("Feedback: player_hurt (exact)");
    trace.string_literal("Feedback: health poll (approx)");
    trace.string_literal("Animstate probe (listen server)");
    trace.string_literal("Chams color##desync_chams_color");
    trace.string_literal("Disable interpolation##no_interp");
    trace.string_literal("Silent: your own view is untouched.");
    trace.string_literal("Tick-quantised animation##tick_anims");
    trace.string_literal("(!) Fake Lag is OFF -- LBY modes need it");
    trace.string_literal("Ghost is off while the model is rebuilt.");
    trace.string_literal("Hold a side on a key instead of letting it alternate.");
    trace.string_literal("How many guesses to build. Each one costs a bone setup.");
    trace.string_literal("Arrows at the crosshair. The lit one is the body side, not the key.");
    trace.string_literal("Press again to release. Back is ignored\\nby Real desync (it already faces away).");
    trace.string_literal("ESP-projected direction lines.\\nExcluded from GTS and streamproof clean captures.");
    trace.string_literal("Master switch for desync visualization.\\nUse ... to configure lines and fake chams separately.");
    trace.string_literal("Never touches the yaw, only flattens a fake pitch. The safe choice\\non servers full of legit players.");
    trace.string_literal("Backwards, flipped left/right once per server update, so their aim\\nlands where you were one update ago.");
    trace.string_literal("Enemy sends pitch +-89 to tilt his whole skeleton. This flattens it\\nto 0 before the hitboxes are built.");
    trace.string_literal("Per-enemy state next to each player: AA/legit verdict, choke,\\ndeg/tick, current guess, misses and hits.");
    trace.string_literal("Where hit/miss comes from. The exact source needs\\n\\\"Subscribe to player_hurt event\\\" under Loggers > DamageLogs.");
    trace.string_literal("Pick the side from cover instead of alternating: the body turns\\ntoward the closer wall. Does nothing in the open.");
    trace.string_literal("Start the search at directions taken from the target (last hit,\\nmovement heading, goal feet yaw) instead of a blind table.");
    trace.string_literal("Build a skeleton per guess and prefer aim points that hit under the\\nmost of them. Live targets only, not backtrack records.");
    trace.string_literal("What \\'backwards\\' and \\'sideways\\' are measured from. Your own view\\nmeans backwards points at anyone you are not looking at.");
    trace.string_literal("Layered on top of the direction instead of replacing it, so\\n\\'backwards + jitter\\' is reachable. Steps once per server update.");
    trace.string_literal("On-screen readout of your own feet yaw (current / goal / delta).\\nUse it to confirm the animstate layout reads correctly in-game.");
    trace.string_literal("Turning the legs alone leaves the chest and head at the twist the\\nclient guessed. This sets the twist the server holds. Leave on.");
    trace.string_literal("Experimental: hook the animation state and let the engine rebuild\\nthe pose instead of rotating it. Mostly covered by Torso twist now.");
    trace.string_literal("Fine-tune the sent tick_count if hits land just\\nahead/behind the enemy. 0 = auto (ping+interp).\\nRaise if shots hit where they WERE, lower if ahead.");
    trace.string_literal("Choked commands steer the server\\'s body, the sent one shows enemies\\nthe far side of it. Holds ~170 deg at any choke depth.\\nNEEDS FAKE LAG -- with nothing choked it is just Backwards.");
    trace.string_literal("Which way the body is turned. The server\\'s hitboxes follow the FEET,\\nso this decides whether the anti-aim does anything at all.\\nAlternate flips every ~0.18s. Freestanding overrides it.");
    trace.string_literal("Replays the enemy\\'s animation for several guesses at the commands\\nwe never received. Does nothing to a MOVING enemy -- the engine pins\\nhis feet to his eyes, so there is nothing to resolve.");
    trace.string_literal("Phase-0 measurement, debug only. Host a listen server or start a map, turn this on, choke a few ticks, then turn it off and read the VERDICT line in the log.\\nDoes nothing at all when server.dll is not in this process.");
    trace.string_literal("Anti-aim normally stops on every tick you hold fire. This keeps it\\nsteering on the ticks the weapon is still on cooldown.\\nOnly works on weapons with an engine fire clock -- the log line\\n[AA-COOLDOWN] says whether it is doing anything.");
    trace.string_literal("How far the six samples sit from the box centre, as a percentage\\nof its half-size.\\n\\nLow = huddled near the centre: safest against a wrong resolve, but\\nfinds fewer exposed slivers. High = out at the faces: finds the\\npeeking edge, but a point near the face leaves the box the moment\\nthe resolve is off. 70%% is the compromise.");
    trace.string_literal("Builds your third-person body at the yaw the SERVER is holding, so what you see is what an enemy\\'s hitboxes are doing.\\nThe engine builds the pose, so the torso twist and the limbs are the server\\'s.\\n\\nOff falls back to Fake chams, which rotates an already-built pose rigidly -- that is why the red copy looks stretched and bent.\\nVisual only: the server is driven by the command angles, which this never touches.");
    trace.string_literal("Do not move the search on an outcome that says nothing about the yaw.\\n\\nTwo cases, both measurable rather than guessed:\\n  * every hypothesis covered the aim point -- they all predict the SAME\\n    outcome, so a miss was not caused by the yaw and a hit does not name\\n    a winner (needs Multi-hypothesis points);\\n  * the target crouched mid-flight -- duck is predicted for you and only\\n    interpolated for him, so that pose was never the server\\'s.\\n\\nThe search gets ONE scored shot per round trip. Spending those on\\nmisses the yaw did not cause walks it away from the right angle exactly\\nas fast as it walks toward it. Off = the old behaviour, charge everything.");
    trace.string_literal("Sample six points around each head/chest/stomach box instead of\\ntrusting the centre and two diagonals.\\n\\nTHE CASE IT FIXES: the head is the chosen group and an arm is in\\nfront of it. With three samples all three trace into the arm, the\\nhead is called invisible, and the aimbot drops a group and shoots\\nthe ARM. A head box is a few units across and a limb rarely covers\\nall of it -- this finds the exposed sliver and keeps the head.\\n\\nCosts traces only when nothing on the preferred group is visible\\nyet: the scan still stops at the first point it can see, and the\\ncentre stays first because it is the most forgiving of a wrong\\nresolve.\\n\\nWith Multi-hypothesis points also on, these extra samples are\\nordered by how many resolver guesses contain them -- that is the\\nreal safe point: one that hits whichever guess turns out right.");
