    trace.string_literal("Queued - loads when you join a game.");
    trace.string_literal("installed sky name (e.g. sky_day01_01)");
    trace.string_literal("Engine loader not found - use Override.");
    trace.string_literal("Calling PopTextWrapPos() too many times!");
    trace.string_literal("Fill model with material##glow_fillmodel");
    trace.string_literal("Beam width in world units (real 3D beam).");
    trace.string_literal("The coloured border around the character.");
    trace.string_literal("Not mounted on this install - drawing Flat.");
    trace.string_literal("Which sky the engine loader binds for your view.");
    trace.string_literal("Lifecycle hooks (PreRender / PostRender / RenderScene)");
    trace.string_literal("Backbuffer mode needs \\\"gmod_mcore_test 0\\\" in console.");
    trace.string_literal("Not applied yet (needs Enable + Custom VTF sky, in game).");
    trace.string_literal("Line width in pixels for 2D, world units for 3D materials.");
    trace.string_literal("Border width in screen pixels - an exact count, not a falloff.");
    trace.string_literal("Type any sky already installed in the game, or import your own VTF below.");
    trace.string_literal("Extra blur passes - widens the ring further. Keep at 1 for a crisp border.");
    trace.string_literal("Move: drag the radar while the menu is open.\\nResize: drag its bottom-right corner grip.");
    trace.string_literal("Players beyond the radar range disappear entirely\\ninstead of sticking to the radar edge.");
    trace.string_literal("Recolors the hands + weapon in first person.\\nHidden from streamproof / screenshots automatically.");
    trace.string_literal("The last hook a per-frame counter can see doubling.\\nCallN\\nClean frame loses Lua screen-space effects.");
    trace.string_literal("Blur radius = how far the ring spreads from the silhouette.\\n~2 for a crisp border, ~5 and up with \\\"Soft glow\\\" on.");
    trace.string_literal("Brightness of the replacement white lightmap.\\n0.45-0.65 usually preserves texture contrast while removing dark areas.");
    trace.string_literal("Refract material: distorts what is BEHIND the model, so the ESP-editor preview can only approximate it. In game it looks right.");
    trace.string_literal("Colours the part of the body that is behind geometry too, in the\\n\\\"hidden\\\" colour. Off = the border only marks what you can actually see.");
    trace.string_literal("Which sky the loose-VMT override points the map\\'s faces at.\\nNothing of ours is written into materials/ for a preset -- only the six VMTs.");
    trace.string_literal("The border is coloured PER PIXEL: the part of the body behind geometry\\ngets the \\\"hidden\\\" colour, the part in line of sight the \\\"visible\\\" one.");
    trace.string_literal("One colour for the whole fill - it is drawn through walls, so there is no\\nvisible/hidden split to make here. The border keeps its own two colours.");
    trace.string_literal("Solid colors: repaints the model.\\nOutline: a coloured border around the character and/or the real\\ntextured model through walls - everything below is switchable.");
    trace.string_literal("Opaque / translucent / viewmodel / player draw hooks.\\nSame CallN risk. The clean frame also loses whatever the\\nSERVER draws in them, so a screengrab looks different.");
    trace.string_literal("Also tint prop / model materials, not just the world brushes.\\nNote: players, NPCs and ragdolls share this material group,\\nso they get tinted too (your own viewmodel is left alone).");
    trace.string_literal("No blur at all. The silhouette is grown by a fixed number of\\npixels and its inside is cut out, so the border is hard-edged and evenly\\nthick instead of fading. Overrides \\\"Soft glow\\\".");
    trace.string_literal("Redraws the player\\'s own textured model with the depth suppressed,\\nso you see the actual body behind geometry. Independent of the border:\\nturn one of the two off for outline-only or model-only.");
    trace.string_literal("Rotating top-down player radar (up = where you look).\\nFrosted-glass background: samples the blurred game screen behind it.\\nDrawn in the ESP overlay -- hidden from OBS / screenshots automatically.");
    trace.string_literal("Tints every world texture client-side (no cvar written).\\nMultiplies the world\\'s color -- pick a dark blue for a \\\"night\\\" look.\\nHidden from OBS / screengrabbers while \\\"Stream-proof view\\\" is on.");
    trace.string_literal("Changes the skybox client-side (no sv_skyname write).\\nEngine loader = presets + any installed sky, native, works on painted maps.\\nHidden from OBS / screengrabbers while \\\"Stream-proof view\\\" is on.");
    trace.string_literal("Engine = native engine sky loader: presets + any installed sky,\\nno material/loose-file footprint, works on painted/VPK maps.\\nOverride = our loose-VMT swap (fallback if the engine signature\\nbreaks after a game update).");
    trace.string_literal("On: the blur bounces through the engine\\'s quarter-size bloom buffer, which\\nsmears the ring far wider than its radius - a soft halo.\\nOff: full-resolution blur, so a small radius leaves a crisp border\\nand no glow at all. Pair \\\"off\\\" with thickness 1-2.");
    trace.string_literal("Draws the model through walls repainted with a chams material -\\nthe same look list \\\"Solid colors\\\" uses - with its own colour and opacity.\\nIndependent of \\\"Show model through walls\\\", which keeps the real texture:\\nwith both on, this one is drawn on top.");
    trace.string_literal("use at own risk!\\nRenders the scene TWICE: a clean first-person pass for the stream, then the cheat view for you.\\nHides freecam/thirdperson/fullbright from OBS Game Capture and RSC/GTS screengrabbers.\\nCosts a second scene render -- tune the cost in the gear settings.");
    trace.string_literal("How often the clean stream frame is re-rendered. Match it to your OBS/record FPS.\\nLower = cheaper (the heavy 2nd render runs this many times/sec instead of every game frame).\\nThis is the main FPS lever: at 30-60 Hz the double-render runs far less often than your game FPS.");
    trace.string_literal("1.00 = the solid chams as before.\\nLower makes the fill see-through - the transparent chams look.\\nWorks with any material; Flat and Additive ghost read best.\\nNote: the viewmodel chams draw from the same material list, so with the\\nsame look selected there they turn see-through too.");
    trace.string_literal("World beam: real 3D, hidden by walls, thickness recedes\\nwith distance. Kept out of screenshots by a check on the\\nrender pass.\\n\\nOverlay: the line is projected and drawn in the ESP overlay,\\nwhich is outside the captured pass by construction - nothing\\nto forget. Draws through walls, flat thickness.");
    trace.string_literal("Also paint UI-panel vgui frames into the OBS capture: Q spawn menu,\\nF1/F4 gamemode menus, context menu, RSC pop-ups.\\nOff = only in-game HUD panels (hp/ammo, scoreboard, chat, net_graph).\\nTrade-off: if you open the Escape (pause) menu while streaming, it will\\nappear in the OBS capture too. Leave ON unless that matters.");
    trace.string_literal("Replaces all six skybox faces with your own VTF from anywhere on disk.\\nAnimated VTFs play (set the FPS below). Picking one face of a 6-face set\\n(*rt.vtf with rt/lf/bk/ft/up/dn siblings) loads the whole set onto the right faces.\\nThe file is copied under garrysmod/materials with a random name; Clear removes it.\\nHidden from OBS / screengrabbers while \\\"Stream-proof view\\\" is on.");
    trace.string_literal("Also skip Lua frame-lifecycle hooks (PreRender / PostRender / RenderScene)\\nin the clean pass. These go through the SIMPLE dispatch which has no\\nbracket calls around it, so skipping is verified-safe.\\neven here: PreDrawSkyBox, PreDrawOpaqueRenderables, PreDrawViewModel\\netc. Those go through CallN which wraps the dispatch in engine bracket calls\\n\\nTurn this ON if a server counts PreRender/RenderScene in addition to HUD hooks.");
    trace.string_literal("Resolution of the clean stream pass, as a %% of your screen (Offscreen mode only).\\nLower = the 2nd render draws fewer pixels = more FPS if you are GPU/fill-bound,\\nat the cost of a softer stream image (upscaled back to full size for OBS/RSC).\\n100%% = identical to your screen. Text/HUD in the stream get blurry below ~70%%.\\n\\nBelow 100%% the clean target also gets a size no engine render target shares,\\nwhich makes the OBS bridge pick it up on the first frame instead of retrying.");
    trace.string_literal("Client-side world lighting.\\nLight = brightness boost (ColorModulate) with a slider.\\nFullBright = true unlit world (selfillum on world brushes), lights dark corners too.\\nCheap = native render.SetLightingMode: touches no materials, no FPS cost, instant on/off.\\nWhite LM = replaces the map lightmap with white while preserving textures and World Tint.\\nConfig Hook = forces nFullbright only inside the engine\\'s normal OverrideConfig call.\\nModes 0-3 are cvar-free and hidden from clean captures; Config Hook is not.");
    trace.string_literal("Offscreen (v5): the clean pass renders into a private render target.\\nWorks with threaded rendering, so your gmod_mcore_test stays as-is.\\nRecommended -- this is the mode that keeps your FPS.\\n\\nBackbuffer (v4): renders both passes into the screen buffer and\\nsnapshots it mid-frame. That only works with SYNCHRONOUS rendering,\\nso it needs \\\"gmod_mcore_test 0\\\" in console -- set by YOU, we never\\ntouch the cvar. While mcore is 1 this mode simply skips the clean\\npass (nothing is published to OBS; your own view is unaffected).");
