    trace.string_literal("Diagnostics for reversing where a value comes from.\\nThey report to the log only.");
    trace.string_literal("Walk _G looking for tables that hold per-player data.\\nA table counts only if connected players are actually\\nfound inside it, so config arrays do not show up.");
    trace.string_literal("Release every cached table reference and walk the paths again.\\nNeeded when an addon replaces the table object itself:\\na type check cannot see that, the replacement is still a table.");
    trace.string_literal("Walks the native NW store and compares every key against the\\nLua route, counting agreements and mismatches. Full detail on\\nthe first pass after you enable it, then only summaries and\\nanything that disagrees.");
    trace.string_literal("For names the server computes instead of storing.\\nExample: a Class D whose netvar holds 16305 but who\\nis shown as D-16305 -> write  D-{id:05d}\\n\\nIf any key in the template is missing, the template\\nyields nothing and the key list is used instead, so it\\ndoubles as its own condition.");
    trace.string_literal("Point the BUILT-IN elements (Nickname, Usergroup, Team/Job)\\nat your own template. Configure a server once here instead of\\ncloning a Netvar element into every layout.\\n\\nThe override feeds the JOB side of both job elements; the team side\\nalways comes from the networked team, so disguise detection keeps\\nworking whatever you put here.");
