    trace.string_literal("Drop from this list (the Steam login cache is untouched).");
    trace.string_literal("Point the game at the account as soon as it is signed in.");
    trace.string_literal("Sign in with the refresh token Steam saved for this account");
    trace.string_literal("Steam Guard: approve the login in the Steam app, or type its code here");
    trace.string_literal("Hand the game its own Steam account back, without signing anything out.");
    trace.string_literal("Steam signed the game\\'s own account out - press Restore, then sign Steam back in.");
    trace.string_literal("Lets Steam keep a login token for this account -\\nthat token is what makes the one-click Switch work later.");
    trace.string_literal("Point the game at the account signed in above.\\n\\\"Auto deploy\\\" already does this after a login or a switch.");
    trace.string_literal("The token names its own account - the username box is only\\na fallback for accounts Steam has never signed in here.");
    trace.string_literal("Signs in with a Steam refresh token instead of a password.\\nThe username field above has to be filled in too - a token\\ncarries no name, and Steam wants both.");
    trace.string_literal("Reads the accounts Steam already remembers (loginusers.vdf)\\ninto the list, and picks up a token for every one Steam still\\nhas cached - those switch with no password at all.\\nNever reads or stores a password.");
    trace.string_literal("Press after a server refused the join with\\n\\\"Steam validation rejected\\\".\\nChecks that Steam has given the account a connect token back,\\nthen drops the stale auth ticket the engine cached for that\\nserver so the next connect asks for a fresh one.\\nIf it says the pool is still empty, wait a few seconds and\\npress again.");
    trace.string_literal("Writes the full account report to the log: licence,\\nownership ticket, connect tokens, running game - and WHO OWNS\\nthe copy of the game. A borrowed (family-shared) copy is what\\nmakes some servers let you in and then throw you out.\\nFree. Ctrl+click also spends one auth ticket and one connect\\ntoken on a live join probe.");
