    trace.string_literal("Skin/body limits appear in-game.");
    trace.string_literal("...more hidden, refine the filter");
    trace.string_literal("Current: %d ms  (avg drop %.1f u)");
    trace.string_literal("Lua / Workshop cache##clean_cache");
    trace.string_literal("Model change is client-side only.");
    trace.string_literal("Disable lua/bin DLLs##clean_luabin");
    trace.string_literal("Hides FreeCam/3rd/Chams from grabs");
    trace.string_literal("Nothing cloaked. Add a path below.");
    trace.string_literal("Restore defaults##fscloak_defaults");
    trace.string_literal("requested %d  spent %d  starved %d");
    trace.string_literal("Re-roll file times##clean_filetimes");
    trace.string_literal("Break lag compensation on rage shots");
    trace.string_literal("Override bodygroups##setskin_body_en");
    trace.string_literal("Reset flagged ConVars##clean_convars");
    trace.string_literal("(!) Start near 1.00 and step outward.");
    trace.string_literal("Also the main-menu realm##fscloak_menu");
    trace.string_literal("Enable local model##tools_model_enable");
    trace.string_literal("Re-roll install age##clean_install_age");
    trace.string_literal("Tap mode (tap to arm, tap to teleport)");
    trace.string_literal("Current model: %d skin(s), body max %d.");
    trace.string_literal("Files saved / duplicates skipped / dropped");
    trace.string_literal("Probes the longest pause this server allows.");
    trace.string_literal("%zu path(s) - hooks arm on the next map load.");
    trace.string_literal("Scrub Lua file paths (debug info)##fscloak_dbg");
    trace.string_literal("discarded bursts: %d (last %.0f%% of expected)");
    trace.string_literal("Unlock (clear blocking flags)##tools_cvar_flags");
    trace.string_literal("Clean net_Disconnect carrying your reason string.");
    trace.string_literal("Userinfo update; the server decides when it shows.");
    trace.string_literal("Click to switch this path between hidden and empty.");
    trace.string_literal("Force value (never touches flags)##tools_cvar_force");
    trace.string_literal("Hide workshop addons (engine.GetAddons)##fscloak_ws");
    trace.string_literal("kills from the event: %d   poll guesses ignored: %d");
    trace.string_literal("Click a token to copy it, then paste it into a message.");
    trace.string_literal("Example:  gg {name}, killed by {myrpname} with {weapon}");
    trace.string_literal("Kills faster than this queue up and drain\\nat this rate.");
    trace.string_literal("Hide other mounted games (engine.GetGames)##fscloak_games");
    trace.string_literal("A pattern matches files, not a folder, so it is always hidden.");
    trace.string_literal("Only crouch for falls this fast.\\nFall damage starts at 580 u/s.");
    trace.string_literal("%zu path(s), %d hook(s)  |  %llu blocked, %llu cut, %llu scrubbed");
    trace.string_literal("Release ticks between synthetic presses.\\n1 = a press every other command.");
    trace.string_literal("Drops clc_Move: no commands, no gravity.\\nPacket still sent, so no timeout.");
    trace.string_literal("Time between random Spam messages.\\nUse a sensible interval for server limits.");
    trace.string_literal("[DUMP] Lua dumper disabled. Files: %d, dupes: %d, dropped: %d, queued: %zu KB\\n");
    trace.string_literal("player_death is not up, which costs nothing\\nhere: a kill is a kill either way.");
    trace.string_literal("When OFF, existing files are protected\\nfrom being replaced by anti-cheat scripts");
    trace.string_literal("Scales host_frametime = ticks per second.\\n1.00 = off. Hotkey bound = hold to apply.");
    trace.string_literal("One command per interval = one tick of fall.\\nShorter is safer; 0 = never (holds ~1s).");
    trace.string_literal("player_death: live -- exact kills only.\\nThe damage poll is OFF and cannot invent one.");
    trace.string_literal("garrysmod/download, downloads and downloadlists --\\nevery file servers made you fastdl.");
    trace.string_literal("player_hurt: live -- a lethal hit the server\\nreported IS the kill. The guessing poll is OFF.");
    trace.string_literal("OFF: models/player only (playermodels).\\nON: the whole models/ tree - slower, thousands of entries.");
    trace.string_literal("Over 14 one packet cannot hold them all (15 cmds\\nmax), so the surplus rides the next one or is lost.");
    trace.string_literal("Auto-jumps on the last tick before you walk off a ledge:\\nfull jump height off every edge, keeps bhop speed.");
    trace.string_literal("Freeze ticks between packets.\\nHigher = slower fall; too high may\\ntime you out. 31 = ideal for all servers.");
    trace.string_literal("Your own .html. Images / CSS / JS next to it load too -\\nits folder is served as the page root, nothing is copied.");
    trace.string_literal("Delay between the crosshair landing on a\\ntarget and the shot. 0 = instant (obvious);\\n120-250ms reads like human reaction.");
    trace.string_literal("Over sv_maxusrcmdprocessticks the server drops\\nthe backlog: 12 ticks = 216u, 32 = only 72u.\\nCap keeps the charge just under it.");
    trace.string_literal("player_death: subscribed, never delivered.\\nThis server has not fired it once, so kills\\ncome from the health poll until it does.");
    trace.string_literal("Says a RANDOM message after a confirmed local kill.\\n{name}, {rpname}, {job}, {weapon}... - see Templates\\ninside Edit messages for the full list.");
    trace.string_literal("Binary Lua modules in garrysmod/lua/bin are a scored\\nindicator on their own. Renamed to *.dll.disabled, not\\ndeleted -- rename them back to restore.");
    trace.string_literal("What the server can still pay for. Refills one tick per tick,\\nspends one per command it processes. A warp is clamped to this,\\nnot to the slider above.");
    trace.string_literal("Everything off by default. A file the game holds open cannot\\nbe deleted -- it gets emptied in place instead (never a .db:\\nthose go through the sql wipe).");
    trace.string_literal("How far below the setting the depth may drop, re-rolled\\nonce per cycle. 0%% means every packet gap is identical\\nforever, which no real connection produces.");
    trace.string_literal("player_death: blocked by Anti-AC ->\\n\\\"Block Event Subscriptions\\\". Kills come\\nfrom the passive health poll instead,\\nwhich guesses the attacker and can be wrong.");
    trace.string_literal("Any page the game\\'s browser can open (http:// https://\\nasset://; a missing scheme gets https:// added).\\nEmpty = block the server\\'s screen, GMod\\'s own is shown.");
    trace.string_literal("crashes/ plus loose *.mdmp / *.dmp next to the exe.\\nA dump written while the cheat was injected contains the\\nfull loaded-module list -- our DLL by name and base address.");
    trace.string_literal("Replaces the loading screen a server shows you.\\nGear = built-in mayrr screen, your own file, or a URL.\\nRewrites the argument in the engine\\'s own menu call - no Lua runs.");
    trace.string_literal("Periodically selects a RANDOM message from the separate Spam list.\\nConsecutive repeats are avoided when the list has several messages.\\nSupports the same {tokens} except the victim ones.");
    trace.string_literal("Send immediately once you have moved more than 64 units\\nwithin one choke cycle. The server refuses to rewind a player\\nacross a jump that large, so choking through one throws away\\nyour own backtrack records.");
    trace.string_literal("When to choke packets. Shot commands are\\nnever choked (fakelag can\\'t eat your shots).\\nAlways: constant. While moving: only above\\n40 u/s. In air: only off the ground.\\nPeek: choke behind cover, flush on exposure.");
    trace.string_literal("On the shot, this many extra commands are sent.\\nThey are full movement ticks, so the server runs\\nthem at once and you also LEAP forward - fewer\\nticks = shorter jump.\\nHold the bind to arm it; unbound = every shot.");
    trace.string_literal("Off by default: no anticheat runs in the menu realm, and GMod\\'s own\\nsave / dupe / demo browsers are file.Find callers there.\\nThe realm you host on is never cloaked at all -- lying to your own\\nserver would break hosting.");
    trace.string_literal("Our own page: map preview, server, gamemode, address,\\nyour SteamID, a transfer log and live progress (files,\\ndata, rate, ETA). Nothing to type - it is written to\\ngarrysmod\\\\html only while the screen is up, then deleted.");
    trace.string_literal("Also ages every loose file in the game root (what\\nfile.Find(\\\"*\\\", \\\"base_path\\\") returns) back by months, so\\n\\\"fresh install\\\" / \\\"reinstall\\\" checks -- oldest file newer\\nthan 1-2 days -- stop firing after a re-download.");
    trace.string_literal("cl_timeout back to 30 (a banned client gets a secret value\\nstored in it) plus net_graph / developer / cl_showpos to 0.\\nWritten natively, so a Lua RunConsoleCommand override never\\nsees it. Applied on the next tick in-game.");
    trace.string_literal("Console write, with the blocking flags cleared first.\\n\\nPicks its own route: for sv_cheats / sv_allowcslua the console\\ncannot work and the flag unlock would crash the game, so Set\\nfalls back to the direct object write on its own.");
    trace.string_literal("The server never tells us it threw a burst away -- our commands\\nwere \\'accepted\\' and the sequence advanced. This counts the only\\nevidence a discard leaves: the burst travelled far less than that\\nmany ticks should have carried you.");
    trace.string_literal("Hold mode: hold key to charge, release = teleport.\\nTap mode: tap once to arm (auto-buffers), tap again\\nto teleport - no holding. Lower ticks = works on\\nmore (strict) servers. Auto-recovers if a server\\nrejects the jump (no more freeze).");
    trace.string_literal("Mouse: steer by turning the mouse.\\nWASD: hold movement keys to gain +\\nsteer; mouse nudges live.\\nCircle: constant turn, hold D = right\\n(default left); tightness 90 = smallest.\\nRage: auto-gains forward, hands-free.\\nGroundstrafe keeps speed between hops.");
    trace.string_literal("Runs the selected file steps again when gmod.exe itself exits.\\nIt is skipped for the cheat\\'s normal unload, so unload/re-inject\\nis unaffected. SQLite and ConVars are not called through game APIs\\nfrom this path; database files are only deleted if no longer locked.");
    trace.string_literal("Randomises the modification time of exactly the four paths\\nthe fingerprint hashes:\\n  garrysmod/gameinfo.txt\\n  garrysmod/lua/autorun/base_vehicles.lua\\n  garrysmod/lights.rad\\n  <root>/sourceengine (the folder itself)\\nThey are the only part of a device fingerprint the client\\nactually controls.");
    trace.string_literal("Hidden = does not exist at all.\\nEmpty  = the folder is still there, it is just never\\n         holding anything (right for addons/: the\\n         folder is stock, the contents are the tell).\\n*  matches within one folder, ** at any depth:\\nlua/*.lua hides loose Lua files sitting in lua/,\\nlua/**.lua hides every .lua under it.");
    trace.string_literal("Crouches through a fall and unducks + jumps on the one command\\nwhere the ground sits 36-38u below you: the engine hands out the\\nground entity before it checks for a landing, so no fall damage is\\never computed - custom OnPlayerHitGround/GetFallDamage included.\\nThe window is 2 units wide, so not every fall lines up; misses land\\nnormally.");
    trace.string_literal("Reports every game except garrysmod as not installed and not\\nmounted. This is a pure fingerprint input -- nova hashes exactly\\nthese flags into its device id.\\n\\nThe list itself is kept, only the flags are cleared: GMod\\'s set of\\nknown games is fixed, so an empty list is an anomaly while\\n\\\"owns nothing but the base game\\\" is the commonest setup there is.");
    trace.string_literal("Paths are relative to garrysmod/, and one rule covers every way\\nof spelling the same folder -- \\\"lua/bin\\\" catches all three of\\nfile.Find(\\\"lua/bin/*\\\",\\\"MOD\\\"), file.Find(\\\"bin/*\\\",\\\"LUA\\\") and\\nfile.Find(\\\"garrysmod/lua/bin/*\\\",\\\"base_path\\\").\\nUse data/... for the data folder, @root/... for what really is\\noutside garrysmod/ (bin/, sourceengine/, the exe).");
    trace.string_literal("garrysmod/data, ALWAYS in full. The ban markers a server\\nwrites there (vcmod_download_data*, stormfox/lightmap_*,\\nvcmod/settings_sh_*, aphone/link_imgur_*, ulx/ulx_log_*,\\nawarn3/client_id_*) carry the server\\'s own random id in the\\nname, so there is nothing stable to pick out -- and the next\\nAC uses six other names anyway.\\nLegit addon settings go with them.");
    trace.string_literal("Lets the rage aim set cl_lagcompensation 0 for shots at a target\\nthe server refuses to rewind, so the shot resolves against where\\nthe target IS. Paired with rage\\'s \\'Extrapolate unreachable\\ntargets\\' -- neither half is worth anything alone.\\n\\nLOUD: cl_lagcompensation is FCVAR_USERINFO, so every flip is a\\nuserinfo update the server can see. Flips are rate-limited to two\\nper second and always restored.");
    trace.string_literal("When Stream-proof view is ON, feed EVERY capture (OBS / RSC / GTS / F12)\\nthe always-ready clean frame the double-render already makes, instead of\\nblanking your visuals for a moment on each grab.\\nStops the on/off micro-stutter a server can trigger by spamming captures --\\nyou keep seeing your cheat, the grab still comes out clean.\\nNeeds Stream-proof view enabled (Effects). No separate OBS Bypass required.");
    trace.string_literal("Takes GameUI\\'s own panel off the loading screen - the grey box in the\\ncorner with \\\"Authenticating with Steam...\\\", the progress bar and Cancel.\\nIt is a vgui popup, so it draws ON TOP of whichever page is set here.\\nOnly the drawing is skipped: Escape still cancels a connect, and its\\nCancel button still works where it used to be. Connection ERRORS use the\\nsame panel and are never hidden, so a failed connect still tells you why.");
    trace.string_literal("engine.GetAddons() returns your whole workshop subscription --\\ntitle, wsid, size, mounted -- and never goes near the filesystem,\\nso nothing above touches it. Entries whose .gma sits under a\\ncloaked path are dropped.\\n\\n(!) With the default addons rule that empties the list, and some\\ngamemodes MOUNT CONTENT from it -- wOS dynabase (Z-City/Homigrad)\\nwalks GetAddons and calls game.MountGMA(addon.file) for models.\\nTurn this on only if you can live without that.");
    trace.string_literal("Puts the built-in list back: addons (empty), lua/bin (hidden),\\nlua/*.lua (hidden).\\n\\nThe last one is precise on purpose -- a stock garrysmod/lua holds\\nonly directories, so a loose .lua sitting there is always\\nsomething that was put there (a dump, an executor\\'s scratch file).\\nA broad lua/* would swallow the stock folders instead and make the\\nwhole tree vanish, which is far louder than the files it hides.\\n\\nReplaces the current list, so a config saved with its own rules\\ngets the defaults back only when you press this.");
    trace.string_literal("file.Find(\\\"addons/*\\\") is the cheapest scan a server can run, and the\\nlisting it returns is a fingerprint of this machine -- every addon you\\nhave, every binary module in lua/bin, every leftover in between.\\n\\nWith this on, the paths in the list below answer as if they were not\\nthere: gone from listings, and Exists / IsDir / Read / Open / Size /\\nTime answer the way they answer for a path that never existed. The\\nengine is untouched -- everything mounted stays mounted, only what\\nLua is TOLD changes.\\n\\nDoes not cover require / include: pcall(include, path) is still an\\nexistence oracle for a .lua file.");
    trace.string_literal("Every function carries the name of the file it came from, and\\ndebug.getinfo / debug.traceback / jit.util.funcinfo hand it over\\nwithout touching a single file API. Walk hook.GetTable() and you\\nhave a list of what is loaded on this client.\\n\\nWith this on, a function whose file matches a rule above reports\\nas a C function: source \\\"=[C]\\\", short_src \\\"[C]\\\", what \\\"C\\\",\\nline numbers -1 -- all of it together, because half a rewrite is\\nan impossible combination and a sharper tell than the leak.\\n\\nChunk names are spelled \\\"lua/<addon-subfolder>/...\\\" or\\n\\\"addons/<name>/...\\\", so the addons rule already covers the\\nsecond; add lua/<folder> for the first.\\n\\nTrade-off: an addon of yours that looks up its OWN path this way\\ngets [C] too. Error message text is not covered - only these\\nthree functions are.");
    trace.string_literal("We run as a DLL inside the ALREADY RUNNING game, so a .db the\\nprocess opened at startup can never be deleted from here.\\nWhat is possible is emptying it through the sqlite connection\\nthat already owns it -- every table dropped, every cookie\\ndeleted -- for cl.db and mn.db. No Lua is involved: the\\nengine\\'s own sqlite3_exec and its database handle are found\\nby signature, and each connection is asked (PRAGMA\\ndatabase_list) which file it just worked on.\\nsv.db is only open while YOU host, so it is deleted outright.\\n\\nGMod\\'s sqlite is built with SQLITE_OMIT_VACUUM: DROP TABLE\\nleaves the old bytes in the freed pages. The wipe therefore\\nrefills the freelist with junk until PRAGMA freelist_count\\nhits 0. Reclaiming the SPACE still needs the game closed.\\nA .db is never truncated -- a zeroed file under a live sqlite\\nhandle is a corrupt database, not a clean one.");
