    trace.string_literal("Drag the feed while the menu is open. My hits / Hits on me / Others filter it too.");
    trace.string_literal("From FireBullets on all players (incl. enemies). Amount/hp shown when the gamemode provides it.");
    trace.string_literal("Folds shots landing back to back on the same target\\ninto one line (\\\"120 x5\\\") instead of one line per pellet.");
    trace.string_literal("Off: the newest line sits on top and older ones slide down.\\nOn: lines are added under the stack, oldest on top.");
    trace.string_literal("On-screen damage feed, top-left by default.\\nDrag it while the menu is open.\\nWorks on its own - the log below can stay off.");
    trace.string_literal("Outgoing net.* captured by name + typed content (passive C hooks, no pcall). \\'view\\' to expand / resend. C logging adds raw engine-level in/out entries.");
    trace.string_literal("Default (off): damage is read from the health netvar we already receive.\\nPassive, nothing is requested from the server, nobody can see it.\\n\\nOn: asks the server to send us its own player_hurt event -> each shotgun\\npellet as its own hit, the attacker straight from the server, and damage\\non players you cannot see (dormant / hidden HP).\\n\\nCost: the subscription sets one bit in our clc_ListenEvents. LSAC ships\\nsourcenet and majority-votes that bitfield across players, so it CAN spot\\nthe odd one out. Pure-Lua anticheats cannot see it at all.\\nBlocked by Aimbot -> Anti-AC -> \\\"Block Event Subscriptions\\\" (on by\\ndefault); turn that sub-toggle off to keep this while Anti-AC stays on.");
