    trace.string_literal("##fc_velocity_decay");
    trace.string_literal("Custom aspect ratio");
    trace.string_literal("Override while zoomed");
    trace.string_literal("%d:%d = %.2f    screen %.2f");
    trace.string_literal("Both axes equal = plain zoom, no stretch");
    trace.string_literal("Back to the centered camera (both offsets 0).");
    trace.string_literal("Positive raises the hands, negative lowers them.");
    trace.string_literal("Positive moves the hands to the right, negative to the left.");
    trace.string_literal("Multiplier of the native aspect ratio.\\n>1 = stretched (wider), <1 = squished.");
    trace.string_literal("Shoulder offset.\\nPositive is to the right, negative to the left, 0 is centered.");
    trace.string_literal("Forward/back is the VM FOV slider.\\nNeeds Viewmodel FOV on; hidden from captures.");
    trace.string_literal("Vertical offset of the camera.\\nPositive looks down from above, negative from below.");
    trace.string_literal("Force the custom FOV even while a weapon scope/zoom is active.\\nOff = scopes keep their normal zoom.");
    trace.string_literal("Sideways only (rides the FOV).\\n>1 = models wider, less visible to the sides. <1 = squished, more visible.");
    trace.string_literal("Up/down only (rides the ratio).\\n>1 = models taller, less visible above/below. <1 = squished, more visible.");
    trace.string_literal("Hands/weapon are drawn in their own pass with a separate FOV.\\nRaise it to pull the viewmodel away from the camera.\\nThe gear also holds the hand position offset.");
    trace.string_literal("The old control: one number scaling the ratio\\nthe screen already has (>1 wider, <1 squished).\\nOff = explicit width:height, which comes out the\\nsame on any monitor.");
    trace.string_literal("Two real, independent axes. A width:height pair\\ncannot do that -- the ratio is a single number,\\nso 16:9 and 32:18 render identically and both\\nfields move the same thing.");
    trace.string_literal("Render the view at an explicit width:height instead of the screen\\'s own.\\nNarrower than the screen = stretched (models look wider), wider = squished.\\nHidden from streamproof captures.");
